   "source": [
    "# Optical Band Gap Prediction for Perovskite Semiconductors\n",
    "\n",
    "## 1. Abstract\n",
    "The optical band gap ($E_g$) is the primary property determining the spectral response and maximum theoretical efficiency (Shockley-Queisser limit) of a solar cell. This notebook demonstrates the training and evaluation of an XGBoost regressor that predicts $E_g$ using atomic and structural descriptors.\n",
    "\n",
    "## 2. Methodology\n",
    "*   **Data:** Enriched perovskite composition dataset.\n",
    "*   **Features:** Ionic radii ($r$), Electronegativity ($en$), Atomic Mass, and Goldschmidt Factors.\n",
    "*   **Model:** XGBoost with Bayesian hyperparameter optimization."
   ],
   "id": "intro"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {
    "ExecuteTime": {
     "end_time": "2026-04-19T21:25:42.324795Z",
     "start_time": "2026-04-19T21:25:42.296064Z"
    }
   },
   "source": [
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import joblib\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "import seaborn as sns\n",
    "from sklearn.metrics import mean_absolute_error, r2_score\n",
    "\n",
    "# NUCLEAR OPTION FOR WHITE BACKGROUNDS\n",
    "import matplotlib as mpl\n",
    "mpl.rcParams['figure.facecolor'] = 'white'\n",
    "mpl.rcParams['axes.facecolor'] = 'white'\n",
    "mpl.rcParams['savefig.facecolor'] = 'white'\n",
    "sns.set_theme(style=\"whitegrid\", palette=\"muted\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Load data\n",
    "df = pd.read_parquet('../data/enriched_perovskites.parquet').dropna(subset=['band_gap'])\n",
    "model = joblib.load('../ml_models/xgboost_band_gap.joblib')\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Loaded {len(df)} samples with band gap values.\")"
   ],
   "id": "load",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Loaded 900 samples with band gap values.\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "execution_count": 4
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3. Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA)\n",
    "We analyze how the chemical composition affects the band gap. A key relationship is usually observed between the **B-site Electronegativity** and the band gap."
   ],
   "id": "eda_md"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {
    "ExecuteTime": {
     "end_time": "2026-04-19T21:25:42.402509Z",
     "start_time": "2026-04-19T21:25:42.327628Z"
    }
   },
   "source": [
    "plt.figure(figsize=(8, 5), facecolor='white')\n",
    "ax = sns.scatterplot(data=df, x='en_B', y='band_gap', hue='tolerance_factor', palette='viridis', alpha=0.6)\n",
    "ax.set_facecolor(\"white\")\n",
    "plt.title(\"Band Gap vs. B-site Electronegativity\", fontsize=14)\n",
    "plt.xlabel(\"Electronegativity (B-site)\", fontsize=12)\n",
    "plt.ylabel(\"Band Gap (eV)\", fontsize=12)\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ],
   "id": "eda_plot",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 800x500 with 1 Axes>"
      ],
      "image/png": ""
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data",
     "jetTransient": {
      "display_id": null
     }
    }
   ],
   "execution_count": 5
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4. Model Performance Evaluation\n",
    "We evaluate the model's accuracy by comparing predicted values against actual experimental data."
   ],
   "id": "eval_md"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {
    "ExecuteTime": {
     "end_time": "2026-04-19T21:25:42.447385Z",
     "start_time": "2026-04-19T21:25:42.405606Z"
    }
   },
   "source": [
    "# Pre-calculate predictions\n",
    "features = ['composition_inorganic', 'A_1', 'A_2', 'A_3', 'B_1', 'C_1', 'C_2', \n",
    "            'en_A', 'mass_A', 'en_B', 'mass_B', 'en_C', 'mass_C', \n",
    "            'tolerance_factor', 'octahedral_factor', 'is_2d', 'dimension', 'space_group']\n",
    "\n",
    "X = df[features]\n",
    "y_true = df['band_gap']\n",
    "y_pred = model.predict(X)\n",
    "\n",
    "mae = mean_absolute_error(y_true, y_pred)\n",
    "r2 = r2_score(y_true, y_pred)\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.figure(figsize=(6, 6), facecolor='white')\n",
    "plt.scatter(y_true, y_pred, alpha=0.4, color='#2c3e50')\n",
    "plt.plot([y_true.min(), y_true.max()], [y_true.min(), y_true.max()], 'r--', lw=2)\n",
    "plt.gca().set_facecolor(\"white\")\n",
    "plt.title(f\"Parity Plot (R² = {r2:.3f})\", fontsize=14)\n",
    "plt.xlabel(\"Experimental Band Gap (eV)\", fontsize=12)\n",
    "plt.ylabel(\"Predicted Band Gap (eV)\", fontsize=12)\n",
    "plt.grid(True, linestyle=':', alpha=0.6)\n",
    "plt.show()\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Mean Absolute Error: {mae:.4f} eV\")"
   ],
   "id": "parity",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 600x600 with 1 Axes>"
      ],
      "image/png": ""
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data",
     "jetTransient": {
      "display_id": null
     }
    },
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Mean Absolute Error: 0.1599 eV\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "execution_count": 6
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 5. Conclusion\n",
    "The model demonstrates high predictive accuracy, suggesting that the integration of **Goldschmidt factors** and **Atomic Weighted properties** is sufficient to capture the electronic trends in hybrid perovskites."
   ],
   "id": "conclusion"
  }
 ],
